# What Vercel uploads is the repo root of a monorepo, and this repo keeps a
# 1.6 GB Python venv and 1.9 GB of local MongoDB state beside the code. Vercel's
# defaults already skip `node_modules` and `.venv`, but not `.local` — which is
# where the mongod data files live, and mongod holds them open, so the upload
# dies with `EBUSY: resource busy or locked, read` before the build even starts.
#
# Excluding local state also keeps the upload small enough to be quick: the
# backend bundle only needs `backend/` minus the venv.

.local/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
backend/.venv/
backend/data/uploads/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/android/
frontend/.vercel/
work/
